  "READ_THIS_FIRST": "THE RAW DISAGREEMENT RATE IS NOT THE FINDING AND MUST NOT BE QUOTED ALONE. 86.2% of decisions have the three seeds disagreeing on sign, but INDEPENDENT signs with these same per-seed marginals would give 84.2% \u2014 so the headline rate is at the chance baseline and carries no information by itself. Reporting 86.2% without the baseline would be inventing alarm. (Self-scaling rule: scale against the statistic's own baseline, never a hand-chosen band.)",
  "THE_ACTUAL_FINDING": "The three seeds carry STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT DIRECTIONAL BIASES. P(mu>0) is 0.3500 / 0.3250 / 0.8625 for seeds 0 / 2 / 4 \u2014 seed 4 is long 86% of the time while seeds 0 and 2 are long about a third of the time. Pairwise sign agreement between seeds 0 and 4 is 0.2625, i.e. they take OPPOSITE directions more often than they agree. Since v1.4.4 established that theta = kappa*c never binds \u2014 traded == scored, and the money-leg IR is a pure function of sign(mu_hat) \u2014 this is the seed instability located at its SOURCE: the -28/-67/-146 IR spread and the 24.4x activity spread are not a subtle downstream artifact, they are three models that disagree about which way to trade.",
